WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.890
The year is 1779.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.750
In a dialogue by David Hume, a sceptic
called Philo asks a sharp question.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.700
If many workers can build one house, why
couldn't several gods combine to make

4
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.200
one world?

5
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.780
Long before Hume, Muslim theologians had
built arguments from the Qur'an's own

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.870
verses.

7
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.200
So does the Qur'an really
argue that God is One,

8
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.200
and do its arguments work?

9
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.860
In this mission, you'll meet the
Qur'an's arguments for one God,

10
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.070
and how theologians set them out.

11
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.620
Then you'll test them against
critics such as Hume and Darwin,

12
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.360
and hear the replies.

13
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.030
Your mission: build the
Qur'an's arguments for one God,

14
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.000
then weigh up whether they work.
